{"timestamp": 1779432059.7522094, "event_type": "body_reported", "tick": 8, "data": {"caller": "player_5", "reason": "Frank reported a dead body", "bodies": [{"room": "medbay", "victim_name": "Diana"}]}}
{"timestamp": 1779432059.7534082, "event_type": "phase_changed", "tick": 8, "data": {"phase": "discussion"}}
{"timestamp": 1779432067.1961684, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 8, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "I found Diana's body dead in Medbay. My route this round was Lower Engine, then I moved through Storage, and finally went up to Medbay to do a task. When I walked in, she was just lying there by the scanner. \n\nI didn't see anyone at all on my way there, and nobody passed me leaving Medbay. Did anyone see who Diana was with earlier, or see anyone heading away from the Medbay/Cafeteria area?"}}
{"timestamp": 1779432082.284026, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 8, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "I started up in Oxygen, then moved down through Upper Engine, and I'm currently in Lower Engine working on a task. Honestly, I haven't seen a single person this entire round. I was completely alone on the left side of the ship.\n\nFrank, since you started in Lower Engine and went right towards Storage, it makes sense we didn't cross paths since I was just arriving at Lower Engine. If you didn't see anyone leaving Medbay, the killer might have vented or gone up towards Cafeteria or right towards Electrical before you got there. \n\nAlice, Charlie, Eve \u2014 where were you guys? Did any of you cross paths near the Cafeteria or center area? Let's hear your routes."}}
{"timestamp": 1779432104.2105863, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 8, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I was in Medbay earlier with Diana \u2014 I can confirm she was alive when I saw her there. I came from Storage, stopped in Medbay for a bit, then left her there and went over to Electrical to do calibrate. I was still in Electrical when the meeting got called.\n\nI didn\u2019t see anyone else in Medbay with her, and nobody came into Electrical while I was there. So if Frank came up from Storage after me and found her, the kill had to be after I left. The only exits would be toward Cafeteria or Electrical, unless the killer doubled back somehow. I\u2019d really like to hear Alice and Charlie\u2019s routes because one of them may have been near center/right side."}}
{"timestamp": 1779432119.1715972, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 8, "data": {"player_id": "player_2", "message": "I started down in Navigation, moved up to Security, and finished my route in Weapons. \n\nI can strongly vouch for Alice for most of the round. Very early on, I saw Alice come into Security from the Electrical side. We then moved up to Weapons together and were both there doing tasks when Frank called the meeting. \n\nEve, your timeline is very interesting. If you saw Diana alive in Medbay and then went to Electrical, that must have been later in the round, because Alice was already out of Electrical and with me on the right side of the ship very early on. Since Alice was with me for the second half of the round, she couldn't have killed Diana if Diana was still alive when you left her. \n\nThat means the killer is almost certainly someone who was near Medbay later in the round \u2014 which points heavily to either Eve (self-report/lying about leaving her alive) or Frank. Bob, your story makes sense for being on the far left.\n\nAlice, when you speak next, please confirm you were with me. Let's see if we can narrow it down between Eve and Frank, or if we should just skip for now to be safe."}}
{"timestamp": 1779432142.0669262, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 8, "data": {"player_id": "player_0", "message": "I can completely confirm Charlie's story. I started my route in Electrical, moved to Security (where I saw Charlie come up from Navigation around tick 3), and then we both headed up to Weapons. We were doing tasks there together when Frank called the meeting. Charlie and I are 100% hard-cleared by each other for the time of the murder.\n\nBecause I started in Electrical and left early on, Eve's story about going to Electrical *after* Medbay does technically fit the timeline \u2014 but it also means she just admitted to being the very last person to see Diana alive. That makes Eve highly suspicious. \n\nHowever, we can't completely rule out a self-report from Frank, or even Bob slipping into Medbay from Upper Engine since he was totally alone and unverified on the left side of the ship. \n\nSince there are 5 of us left and only 1 Duck, we have a buffer. We don't need to risk a 33% guess between Eve, Frank, and Bob right now. I'm going to vote to skip. Charlie, you and I should stick together again next round. If anyone else wants to be cleared, come find us. \n\nskip"}}
{"timestamp": 1779432149.6656957, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 8, "data": {"player_id": "player_5", "message": "skip"}}
{"timestamp": 1779432155.9400532, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 8, "data": {"player_id": "player_1", "message": "skip"}}
{"timestamp": 1779432168.7616432, "event_type": "discussion_message", "tick": 8, "data": {"player_id": "player_4", "message": "I get why I look suspicious as last person to see Diana, but I really did leave her alive in Medbay and went straight to Electrical. I was on calibrate when the report happened. If I were the killer, I don\u2019t think I\u2019d openly say \u201cyeah I was with her in Medbay\u201d when nobody had even placed me there yet.\n\nCharlie/Alice being together makes sense to me, so I\u2019m not pushing there. Frank reporting from Medbay and Bob being alone on left are the only other question marks, but with 5 alive I agree skip is safest rather than guessing wrong. Next round I\u2019m fine grouping with Alice/Charlie or being watched on tasks."}}
